winex11: Add a per-application opt-out from requesting _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW.

MapleStory TW steals the desktop focus back every few seconds.  Click on
anything else -- a browser, a terminal -- and the game is in front again a
moment later, which makes the machine unusable while the game is open.  The
game itself is not doing anything unusual: it calls SetForegroundWindow() on
its own windows continuously (the main window and the embedded NxOverlay web
view both do it).  What changed is what winex11 does with such a call.

wine-10.0 (the base CrossOver ships, on which this game does not steal focus):

    X11DRV_SetFocus()               dlls/winex11.drv/event.c:1281
        if (!data->managed || data->embedder) set_input_focus( data );

  For a window the window manager manages -- every top-level window here --
  it does nothing at all.  The activation stays inside wine; the X focus and
  the WM's idea of the active window are never touched.  wine-10.0's winex11
  never sends _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW at all: grep finds no sender in the whole
  driver.

wine-10.16:

    X11DRV_ActivateWindow()         dlls/winex11.drv/event.c:1344
        if (!is_virtual_desktop()) set_net_active_window( hwnd, previous );
    set_net_active_window()         dlls/winex11.drv/window.c:1946
        xev.xclient.data.l[0] = 2;  /* source: pager */

  Every activation now asks the window manager to make the window active, and
  it asks as a pager.  KWin (and others) treat a pager request as a direct
  user action and grant it unconditionally, bypassing focus stealing
  prevention entirely.  A program that activates itself in a loop therefore
  owns the desktop focus.

There is no way to ask this game to stop, so this adds a way to tell winex11
not to ask the window manager, which is the 10.0 behaviour.  The check goes at
the top of set_net_active_window() rather than at its callers: both call sites
(event.c:1258 when a window is mapped while it is the foreground window, and
event.c:1348 on activation) go through this one function, and any future one
will too.  Activation inside wine is unaffected; so is set_input_focus() for
unmanaged and embedded windows.

The key is read through the existing X11 Driver option mechanism, so it can be
set per application:

    [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\MapleStory.exe\X11 Driver]
    "RequestNetActiveWindow"="N"

The default is "Y" -- unset, every application behaves exactly as before.

Measured on this machine on 2026-09-14, by sampling the owning process of
_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW once a second for 30s after switching the focus away once
(tools/dev/focustest.sh; no other action is taken, nothing is ever re-activated):

    ours, key absent (upstream behaviour)   28/30 samples back on the game
                                                 (first one 1s after switching away)
    ours, "RequestNetActiveWindow"="N"       0/30
    CrossOver's wine-10.0 build              0/30

The same A/B, on the same build, with a probe whose whole body is a window plus
SetForegroundWindow() on itself twice a second (tools/dev/focusthief.c).  This takes
the game, its overlay, its anti-cheat and its login server out of the picture,
and leaves the registry key as the only difference between the two runs:

    probe, key absent                       30/30
    probe, "RequestNetActiveWindow"="N"      0/30

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1949,6 +1949,12 @@
     Window window;
     XEvent xev;
 
+    /* Some applications call SetForegroundWindow() on themselves over and over.  On a
+     * window manager that honours a pager request unconditionally that steals the desktop
+     * focus away from whatever the user is doing.  "RequestNetActiveWindow"="N" in the
+     * per-application X11 Driver key restores the wine 10.0 behaviour for such a program:
+     * managed windows are then activated inside wine only, without asking the WM. */
+    if (!request_net_active_window) return;
     if (!is_net_supported( x11drv_atom(_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW) )) return;
     if (!(window = X11DRV_get_whole_window( hwnd ))) return;
     if (data->pending_state.net_active_window == window) return;
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h
@@ -456,6 +456,7 @@
 extern BOOL usexvidmode;
 extern BOOL use_egl;
 extern BOOL use_take_focus;
+extern BOOL request_net_active_window;
 extern BOOL use_primary_selection;
 extern BOOL use_system_cursors;
 extern BOOL grab_fullscreen;
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv_main.c
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@
 BOOL usexcomposite = TRUE;
 BOOL use_egl = FALSE;
 BOOL use_take_focus = TRUE;
+BOOL request_net_active_window = TRUE;
 BOOL use_primary_selection = FALSE;
 BOOL use_system_cursors = TRUE;
 BOOL grab_fullscreen = FALSE;
@@ -463,6 +464,9 @@
     if (!get_config_key( hkey, appkey, "UseTakeFocus", buffer, sizeof(buffer) ))
         use_take_focus = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
 
+    if (!get_config_key( hkey, appkey, "RequestNetActiveWindow", buffer, sizeof(buffer) ))
+        request_net_active_window = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
+
     if (!get_config_key( hkey, appkey, "UsePrimarySelection", buffer, sizeof(buffer) ))
         use_primary_selection = IS_OPTION_TRUE( buffer[0] );
 
